#: phasex64-panel:307
msgid "Records OUT 3/4 output (analog, incl. Direct)"
msgstr ""

#: phasex64-panel:308
msgid "Records OUT 1/2 output (analog, incl. Direct)"
msgstr ""

#: phasex64-panel:312
msgid ""
"Capturing Out 3/4's own analog output stage (Direct + PCM as routed) - "
"hardware-confirmed, not a copy of In 3/4. Roughly 0.3-0.8 dB lower than the "
"source, down to the analog noise floor (~-85 dBFS) when Out 3/4 is silent. "
"Different signal from capture channels 5/6, which only ever reflect Out "
"1/2's digital PCM content, pre-Direct. If a track in your DAW monitors this "
"input back to Out 3/4, turn off that track's input monitoring - otherwise "
"it's a feedback loop."
msgstr ""

#: phasex64-panel:321
msgid ""
"Capturing Out 1/2's own analog output stage (Direct + PCM as routed) - "
"presumed, not independently hardware-tested (Loopback 3/4's own behaviour "
"was; see analysis/loopback-and-monitoring.md). If a track in your DAW "
"monitors this input back to Out 1/2, turn off that track's input monitoring "
"- otherwise it's a feedback loop."
msgstr ""

#: phasex64-panel:335
msgid "Capture 5/6 = Loopback Out 1/2 (digital, PCM only, pre-Direct)"
msgstr ""

#: phasex64-panel:337
msgid ""
"Always-on digital tap of the PCM/DSP data sent to Out 1/2, bit-exact, before "
"the Direct/PCM output mixing stage - not affected by the Direct or PCM Out "
"1/2 switches, and not the same mechanism as the Loopback capture sources "
"(which are analog and after that mixing stage). No ALSA control of its own - "
"available directly in a 6-channel capture stream (In 1/2, In 3/4, 5/6). See "
"linux/README.md, \"PipeWire / JACK\" and \"Recording what you hear\", for "
"how to use it."
msgstr ""

#: phasex64-panel:355
msgid "Feedback loop: both loopbacks + Direct on both outputs"
msgstr ""

#: phasex64-panel:357
msgid ""
"Both Loopback sources selected with Direct on for both outputs closes an "
"analog loop (In 1/2 -> Direct -> Out 1/2 -> Loopback -> In 3/4 -> Direct -> "
"Out 3/4 -> Loopback -> In 1/2) - hardware-confirmed to raise both inputs to "
"about -68.7 dBFS (vs. an ~-85 dBFS floor with the loop open). Only noise at "
"unity gain, but it can ring/oscillate if gain goes up. Turn off Direct on "
"one output, or use only one Loopback source, to break the loop."
msgstr ""

